{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"WebSite","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/#website","url":"https://www.savvywealth.com/","name":"Savvy Wealth"},{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/jeff-brimhall/#webpage","name":"Jeff Brimhall, PhD, CFP®, CFA: Managing Partner / Wealth Manager in Orem, UT | Savvy Wealth","url":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/jeff-brimhall","description":"Jeff Brimhall, PhD, CFP®, CFA is a Managing Partner at Blue Barn Wealth helping individuals and families simplify financial complexity through planning, tax strategy, and investment management.","isPartOf":{"@type":"WebSite","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/#website"},"primaryImageOfPage":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6479cdbae84fd9792129c576/69a09989eafb8544f9e9343d_60980ede3d654a819c963cb4d5473799_Jeff%20B%20SEO.webp"},"datePublished":"2026-03-09T16:39:44.375Z","dateModified":"2026-03-09T16:39:44.375Z","about":{"@type":"Person","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/jeff-brimhall/#person","name":"Jeff Brimhall","url":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/jeff-brimhall"}},{"@type":"Organization","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/#organization","name":"Savvy Wealth","url":"https://www.savvywealth.com/","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6479cdbae84fd9792129c576/647dd6624b8fd164bb0f9637_Savvy%20Logo.svg"},"sameAs":["https://www.linkedin.com/company/savvywealth","https://x.com/SavvyWealthInc"],"contactPoint":[{"@type":"ContactPoint","telephone":"+1-833-745-6789","contactType":"Customer Service","areaServed":"US","availableLanguage":["English"]}]},{"@type":"Person","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/jeff-brimhall/#person","name":"Jeff Brimhall","honorificSuffix":"PhD, CFP®, CFA","jobTitle":"Managing Partner / Wealth Manager","image":"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6479cdbae84fd9792129c576/69a099805c8ea40ba46bad1d_Jeff%20B%20Hero%20(1).webp","url":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/jeff-brimhall","email":"mailto:jeff@bluebarnwealth.com","telephone":"+1-801-797-1949","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Orem","addressRegion":"UT","addressCountry":"US"},"worksFor":{"@type":"Organization","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/#organization"},"sameAs":["https://www.linkedin.com/in/jefftbrimhall/"],"knowsAbout":["Financial Planning & Analysis","Tax Optimization","Alternative Investing","Investment Management"],"description":"Jeff Brimhall is a managing partner at Blue Barn Wealth, where he enjoys working with clients to simplify their life and master their finances. Prior to Blue Barn Wealth, Jeff served as a Senior Advisor at Soltis Investment Advisors and acted as interim CEO of Ampelis, a corporate and family consulting company focused on successful transitions of culture and assets between generations.

Earlier in his career, Jeff was an award-winning faculty member in Finance and Economics at Case Western Reserve University, an equity analyst in National City Bank’s Private Client Group, and held analyst and advisory roles at Lee Financial, a Registered Investment Advisor in Dallas, TX, and Crow Holdings.

Jeff earned a PhD in Economics from Southern Methodist University and a B.S. in Civil and Environmental Engineering from Brigham Young University. He is a CERTIFIED FINANCIAL PLANNER™ professional and holds the Chartered Financial Analyst designation. Jeff has also served as Chairman of the Utah Chapter of the Financial Planning Association and taught in the Personal Financial Planning Program at Utah Valley University."},{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://www.savvywealth.com"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Jeff Brimhall","item":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/jeff-brimhall"}]},{"@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How did you become a financial advisor?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"I wanted a career that truly made a difference in how people live their lives. My path started as an engineer where I realized I wanted to have a more personal impact on people’s lives, which led me to economics and finance, including work in academia and investment analysis. Over time I became more drawn to helping individuals and families apply these principles in real life. Financial planning gave me the opportunity to combine strategy and relationships in a way that helps people make better decisions and live more intentionally."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What types of clients do you work with?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"My ideal clients are individuals and families who want to use their wealth to make their life, family, community, and the world better. Many are navigating growing complexity—whether that’s investments, career income, taxes, family planning, or long-term legacy goals—and want clarity and structure."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What areas of expertise do you have?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"My background includes investments, financial planning, tax planning, charitable giving, legacy planning, and alternative investments. I also work with clients who want a more comprehensive approach—where planning, investments, and long-term goals all fit together."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What types of strategies do you usually help clients with?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"We offer a comprehensive planning process built around key areas such as financial planning, investment management, tax planning, estate planning, and charitable giving. The goal is to help clients make confident decisions across all parts of their financial life, not just one piece at a time."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is there a unique approach that sets you apart?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"We truly offer comprehensive services. I bring a combination of academic training, real-world investment experience, and advisory work, with a focus on simplifying complexity. Clients shouldn’t feel overwhelmed by their finances—they should feel confident, informed, and supported by a clear strategy."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is your favorite part about working with clients?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Getting to know what is most important to clients—what they most want to accomplish in their life—and helping them make that happen. Helping people move from uncertainty to clarity is incredibly rewarding."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Working with Savvy","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"I chose to work with Savvy to enhance the services and capabilities we offer our clients. Savvy provides stronger technology and operational support behind the scenes, which allows us to operate more efficiently and deliver a higher level of client service—while staying focused on what matters most: our clients and their goals."}}]}]}

{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"WebSite","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/#website","url":"https://www.savvywealth.com/","name":"Savvy Wealth"},{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/justin-ericksen/#webpage","name":"Justin Ericksen, CFP®, CFA, AFC®: Wealth Manager in Orem, UT | Savvy Wealth","url":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/justin-ericksen","description":"Justin Ericksen, CFP®, CFA, AFC® is an advisor at Blue Barn Wealth helping individuals and families build financial clarity through planning, investment strategy, and wealth management.","isPartOf":{"@type":"WebSite","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/#website"},"primaryImageOfPage":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6479cdbae84fd9792129c576/69a09c2f5e0d8e02864de9ce_2f46bc32b28e461dcfef00304583efaa_Justin%20E%20SEO.webp"},"datePublished":"2026-03-09T16:51:31.884Z","dateModified":"2026-03-09T16:51:31.884Z","about":{"@type":"Person","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/justin-ericksen/#person","name":"Justin Ericksen","url":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/justin-ericksen"}},{"@type":"Organization","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/#organization","name":"Savvy Wealth","url":"https://www.savvywealth.com/","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6479cdbae84fd9792129c576/647dd6624b8fd164bb0f9637_Savvy%20Logo.svg"},"sameAs":["https://www.linkedin.com/company/savvywealth","https://x.com/SavvyWealthInc"],"contactPoint":[{"@type":"ContactPoint","telephone":"+1-833-745-6789","contactType":"Customer Service","areaServed":"US","availableLanguage":["English"]}]},{"@type":"Person","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/justin-ericksen/#person","name":"Justin Ericksen","honorificSuffix":"CFP®, CFA, AFC®","jobTitle":"Wealth Manager","image":"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6479cdbae84fd9792129c576/69a09c2ec8c56e2e73abe551_Justin%20E%20Hero%20(1).webp","url":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/justin-ericksen","email":"mailto:justin@bluebarnwealth.com","telephone":"+1-801-797-1947","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Orem","addressRegion":"UT","addressCountry":"US"},"worksFor":{"@type":"Organization","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/#organization"},"sameAs":["https://www.linkedin.com/in/justin-ericksen-ms-cfp%C2%AE-cfa-afc%C2%AE-492b1216b/"],"knowsAbout":["Financial Planning & Analysis","Alternative Investing","Tax Optimization","Investment Management"],"description":"Justin Ericksen is an Advisor at Blue Barn Wealth and a CERTIFIED FINANCIAL PLANNER™ professional. He also holds the Chartered Financial Analyst designation and earned a master’s degree in Financial Planning and Analytics from Utah Valley University.

Justin is passionate about finance and helping individuals succeed. He believes the most important things in life are spending time with the people you love and enriching the lives of others. His planning philosophy reflects those values—helping clients build financial strategies that support what matters most to them.

Outside of work, Justin enjoys spending time with his wife and siblings. His favorite activities include tennis, snowboarding, singing, and playing board games. Justin, his wife, and their dog live in Fairview, Utah."},{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://www.savvywealth.com"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Justin Ericksen","item":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/justin-ericksen"}]},{"@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How did you become a financial advisor?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"I’ve always been drawn to finance and the role it plays in shaping people’s lives. I pursued formal education in financial planning and analytics and earned both the CFP® and CFA designations to provide clients with comprehensive, disciplined guidance. I wanted a career where I could help people succeed and make confident decisions about their future."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What types of clients do you work with?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"I work with individuals and families who want clarity around their financial direction—whether that’s building wealth, planning for retirement, managing investments, or navigating life transitions."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What areas of expertise do you have?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"My background includes comprehensive financial planning, investment management, and long-term wealth strategy. I focus on aligning investment decisions with a broader financial plan."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What types of strategies do you usually help clients with?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"I help clients develop personalized investment strategies, retirement plans, tax-aware planning approaches, and coordinated financial strategies designed to support their long-term goals."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is there a unique approach that sets you apart?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Holding both the CFP® and CFA designations allows me to approach planning from both a holistic and analytical perspective. I believe strong financial decisions require both a thoughtful plan and disciplined execution."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is your favorite part about working with clients?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Helping clients gain confidence in their financial decisions. When someone feels clear and steady about their financial future, it allows them to focus more fully on the parts of life that matter most."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Working with Savvy","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Partnering with Savvy enhances the tools and support behind the scenes, allowing us to operate more efficiently and deliver a higher level of client service. The additional technology and operational platform enable us to focus even more on thoughtful planning and investment management for the families we serve."}}]}]}

{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"WebSite","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/#website","url":"https://www.savvywealth.com/","name":"Savvy Wealth"},{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/jennifer-gugliemotto/#webpage","name":"Jennifer Gugliemotto: Wealth Manager in Columbus, OH | Savvy Wealth","url":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/jennifer-gugliemotto","description":"Jennifer Gugliemotto is a wealth manager at Savvy Wealth who helps individuals and business owners navigate life transitions with clarity, empathy, and purpose. Her work focuses on financial planning, legacy considerations, risk management, and charitable strategies.","isPartOf":{"@type":"WebSite","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/#website"},"primaryImageOfPage":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6479cdbae84fd9792129c576/691457b79ccfff7c6eccc537_Jeniffer%20G%20Hero%20(3).webp"},"datePublished":"2025-12-19T02:15:23.812Z","dateModified":"2025-12-19T02:15:23.812Z"},{"@type":"Organization","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/#organization","name":"Savvy Wealth","url":"https://www.savvywealth.com/","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6479cdbae84fd9792129c576/647dd6624b8fd164bb0f9637_Savvy%20Logo.svg"},"sameAs":["https://www.linkedin.com/company/savvywealth","https://x.com/SavvyWealthInc"],"contactPoint":[{"@type":"ContactPoint","telephone":"+1-833-745-6789","contactType":"Customer Service","areaServed":"US","availableLanguage":["English"]}]},{"@type":"Person","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/jennifer-gugliemotto/#person","name":"Jennifer Gugliemotto","jobTitle":"Wealth Manager","image":"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6479cdbae84fd9792129c576/691457b79ccfff7c6eccc537_Jeniffer%20G%20Hero%20(3).webp","url":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/jennifer-gugliemotto","email":"mailto:jennifer.gugliemotto@savvyadvisors.com","telephone":"+1-614-733-8835","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Columbus","addressRegion":"OH","addressCountry":"US"},"worksFor":{"@type":"Organization","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/#organization"},"sameAs":["https://www.linkedin.com/in/jennifer-gugliemotto-carl-9598709/"],"knowsAbout":["Financial Planning","Estate & Trust Planning","Risk Management","Legacy & Charitable Planning"],"description":"Jennifer transitioned into financial planning after a profound personal loss reshaped her sense of purpose. Following a 12-year career as a global corporate retail designer, she redirected her creative and analytical skills toward helping others navigate grief, legacy, and complex financial decisions with clarity and compassion.

With seven years of experience in financial planning, including roles at Edward Jones and Huntington Bank, Jennifer now serves clients nationwide through Savvy’s tech-forward, client-centric platform. Her approach emphasizes deep listening, empathy, and flexible engagement—combining in-person and digital collaboration.

Jennifer is actively involved with 4-H, the Columbus Museum of Art’s fundraising initiatives, and alumni organizations for DAAP and Walnut Hills High School. Outside of work, she prioritizes balance, community connection, and continued personal growth."},{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://www.savvywealth.com"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Jennifer Gugliemotto","item":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/jennifer-gugliemotto"}]},{"@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How did you become a financial advisor?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The pivot point in my career came when my best friend, Ruth, passed away from colon cancer at the age of 32. That loss reshaped my purpose and ultimately led me to financial planning as a way to support others through life’s most difficult transitions."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What types of clients do you work with?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"I work with individual investors and business owners, helping them gain clarity, control, and peace of mind as they navigate pivotal life changes."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What areas of expertise do you have?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"My work spans comprehensive financial planning, retirement readiness, estate and charitable planning, risk management, and strategies designed to protect and distribute assets in alignment with each client’s unique life path."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What types of strategies do you usually help clients with?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"I help clients create clarity and fill in the gaps by listening deeply and meeting them where they are. My goal is to add structure, awareness, and long-term guidance through all of life’s transitions."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is there a unique approach that sets you apart?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"My approach is approachable, open-minded, and deeply attentive. I partner with clients in a way that respects their individual needs and emotional context."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is your favorite part about working with clients?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Getting to know their prismatic, multi-dimensional selves."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Working with Savvy","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Savvy’s technology-forward approach aligns with what many of my clients have long wanted. The firm values people, perspective, and innovation, and its vision reflects the future of finance in a digital world."}}]}]}

{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"WebSite","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/#website","url":"https://www.savvywealth.com/","name":"Savvy Wealth"},{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/steven-harp/#webpage","name":"Steven Harp, CFP®, ChFC®, CLU®, AIF®, and CLTC®: Wealth Manager in Denver, CO | Savvy Wealth","url":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/steven-harp","description":"Webpage with info on Steven Harp, wealth manager at Savvy.","isPartOf":{"@type":"WebSite","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/#website"},"primaryImageOfPage":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6479cdbae84fd9792129c576/696fc0a0ff97df075038395e_Steven%20H%20Hero%20(1)-p-500.webp"},"datePublished":"2026-01-29T15:56:25.702Z","dateModified":"2026-01-29T15:56:25.702Z"},{"@type":"Organization","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/#organization","name":"Savvy Wealth","url":"https://www.savvywealth.com/","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6479cdbae84fd9792129c576/647dd6624b8fd164bb0f9637_Savvy%20Logo.svg"},"sameAs":["https://www.linkedin.com/company/savvywealth","https://x.com/SavvyWealthInc"],"contactPoint":[{"@type":"ContactPoint","telephone":"+1-833-745-6789","contactType":"Customer Service","areaServed":"US","availableLanguage":["English"]}]},{"@type":"Person","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/steven-harp/#person","name":"Steven Harp","honorificSuffix":"CFP®, ChFC®, CLU®, AIF®, and CLTC®","jobTitle":"Wealth Manager","image":"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6479cdbae84fd9792129c576/696fc0a0ff97df075038395e_Steven%20H%20Hero%20(1)-p-500.webp","url":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/steven-harp","email":"mailto:sharp@coloradowealthgroup.com","telephone":"+1-720-729-2501","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Denver","addressRegion":"CO","addressCountry":"US"},"worksFor":{"@type":"Organization","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/#organization"},"sameAs":["https://www.linkedin.com/in/stevenharp/"],"knowsAbout":["Retirement Planning","Financial Planning","Tax Optimization","Investment Management"],"description":"Steven Harp is the Founder and Chief Executive Officer of Colorado Wealth Group. He graduated from the University of Missouri in 2004 and has since built an advisory practice grounded in fiduciary responsibility, education, and personalized service.

Steven is a CERTIFIED FINANCIAL PLANNER® professional and holds several advanced industry designations, including ChFC®, CLU®, AIF®, and CLTC®. These credentials support comprehensive guidance across investments, retirement planning, tax planning, insurance, estate considerations, and long-term care strategies.

In addition to serving clients, Steven is passionate about continuing education and mentoring, helping develop advisors within Colorado Wealth Group to ensure consistent, high-quality client experiences."},{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://www.savvywealth.com"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Steven Harp","item":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/steven-harp"}]},{"@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How did you become a financial advisor?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"I graduated from the University of Missouri in 2004 and began my career with a strong interest in helping people make confident, informed financial decisions. Over time, that interest evolved into a passion for comprehensive financial planning and fiduciary advice. Building Colorado Wealth Group has allowed me to combine that passion with a commitment to education, leadership, and long-term client relationships."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What types of clients do you work with?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"I work with individuals and families who want a thoughtful, personalized approach to managing their wealth. Many of my clients value long-term planning, proactive guidance, and a trusted advisor who can help them navigate life transitions with clarity and confidence."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What areas of expertise do you have?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"My expertise lies in comprehensive financial planning, including investment management, retirement planning, risk management, estate considerations, and long-term care planning. I take a holistic view of each client’s financial life to ensure every decision works together toward their goals."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What types of strategies do you usually help clients with?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"I help clients develop strategies focused on long-term financial security—retirement income planning, investment allocation, insurance and risk management, and planning for healthcare and long-term care needs. Every strategy is customized to reflect each client’s priorities and circumstances."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is there a unique approach that sets you apart?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"As a fiduciary, my approach is centered on objectivity, education, and personalization. I believe financial planning should be transparent and collaborative. Clients should understand their options, feel confident in their decisions, and know their advisor is always acting in their best interest."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Working with Savvy","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Savvy’s platform supports the high-touch, fiduciary-focused service model we value at Colorado Wealth Group. Its modern technology, collaborative resources, and integrated planning tools allow us to deliver a seamless client experience while keeping the focus on clients’ goals."}}]}]}

{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"WebSite","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/#website","url":"https://www.savvywealth.com/","name":"Savvy Wealth"},{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/bruce-larsen/#webpage","name":"Bruce Larsen, CEP®, NSSA®, EA: Wealth Manager in Denver, CO | Savvy Wealth","url":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/bruce-larsen","description":"Webpage with info on Bruce Larsen, wealth manager at Savvy.","isPartOf":{"@type":"WebSite","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/#website"},"primaryImageOfPage":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6479cdbae84fd9792129c576/6970b4b30338ee01bac7f48c_Bruce%20Larsen%20SEO.webp"},"datePublished":"2026-01-29T16:12:03.269Z","dateModified":"2026-01-29T16:12:03.269Z"},{"@type":"Organization","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/#organization","name":"Savvy Wealth","url":"https://www.savvywealth.com/","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6479cdbae84fd9792129c576/647dd6624b8fd164bb0f9637_Savvy%20Logo.svg"},"sameAs":["https://www.linkedin.com/company/savvywealth","https://x.com/SavvyWealthInc"],"contactPoint":[{"@type":"ContactPoint","telephone":"+1-833-745-6789","contactType":"Customer Service","areaServed":"US","availableLanguage":["English"]}]},{"@type":"Person","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/bruce-larsen/#person","name":"Bruce Larsen","honorificSuffix":"CEP®, NSSA®, EA","jobTitle":"Wealth Manager","image":"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6479cdbae84fd9792129c576/696fd8cd17cb6fbf43c77f58_Bruce%20L%20Hero%20(1)-p-500.webp","url":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/bruce-larsen","email":"mailto:blarsen@coloradowealthgroup.com","telephone":"+1-720-729-2078","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Denver","addressRegion":"CO","addressCountry":"US"},"worksFor":{"@type":"Organization","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/#organization"},"sameAs":["https://www.linkedin.com/in/bruce-larsen-54392530a/"],"knowsAbout":["Retirement Planning","Financial Planning","Estate & Trust Planning"],"description":"Bruce Larsen has been in the financial services industry for over 30 years. He began his career after graduating from the University of Wyoming in 1988 with a BS in Accounting, spending nearly a decade in accounting, including time as a corporate CFO. In 2020, Bruce brought his practice to Colorado Wealth Group to expand his ability to collaborate, mentor, and continue his passion for helping clients organize and understand their financial lives.

Over the years, his practice has evolved to take a multi-generational approach, working with clients and their families across different life stages. He has written a book on taxes and holds the Certified Estate Planner™ (CEP®) designation, focusing on estate planning essentials such as living trusts, estate taxes, and disability or special needs planning. Bruce is also an Enrolled Agent (EA), licensed to represent clients before the IRS.

Bruce grew up on a cattle ranch in Wyoming and has made Colorado his home with his wife, Cindy, since 2008. They have two grown children. Outside of work, Bruce trains horses and participates in team roping events."},{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://www.savvywealth.com"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Bruce Larsen","item":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/bruce-larsen"}]},{"@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How did you become a financial advisor?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"My career began in accounting, eventually leading to a corporate CFO role. Over time, I found myself wanting to work more directly with individuals and families, helping them make sense of their finances in a way that felt accessible and personal. That desire prompted my transition into financial advising, where retirement and tax planning became central parts of my work."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What types of clients do you work with?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"I primarily work with people who are at or nearing retirement. Many are preparing for major financial transitions, evaluating their income needs, or working through estate and legacy considerations. I also collaborate with families across generations, helping them stay organized and aligned as their circumstances evolve."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What areas of expertise do you have?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"My background includes tax planning, estate planning, and retirement planning. These areas often overlap, and I enjoy helping clients understand how decisions in one area influence the others. My training as a CEP® and my work as an Enrolled Agent contribute to the technical foundation I bring to each relationship."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What types of strategies do you usually help clients with?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"I assist clients with Social Security filing considerations, tax-aware planning, retirement income planning, and estate and trust planning. These strategies are guided by a client’s goals, family structure, and long-term needs, and I take a holistic look at how each piece fits into the broader picture."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is there a unique approach that sets you apart?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"I tend to start with taxes. It often provides a useful framework for understanding someone’s overall situation, and it helps reveal opportunities or considerations that might otherwise be overlooked. That tax-first perspective has been part of my approach since the beginning of my work in financial planning."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is your favorite part about working with clients?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"I enjoy catching up with clients and learning how their lives and priorities are evolving. Those conversations help shape the guidance I provide and strengthen long-term relationships. Seeing clients gain clarity and a stronger sense of direction is one of the most rewarding parts of this work."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Working with Savvy","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"I appreciate the high level of support Savvy provides — from technology to operational resources — which helps create a smoother experience for both advisors and clients."}}]}]}

{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"WebSite","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/#website","url":"https://www.savvywealth.com/","name":"Savvy Wealth"},{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/nathan-mirizzi/#webpage","name":"Nathan Mirizzi, CFP®: Wealth Manager in Salt Lake City, UT | Savvy Wealth","url":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/nathan-mirizzi","description":"Nathan Mirizzi, CFP® is an Associate Advisor at Blue Barn Wealth helping individuals and families build financial clarity through planning, investment strategy, and guidance.","isPartOf":{"@type":"WebSite","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/#website"},"primaryImageOfPage":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6479cdbae84fd9792129c576/69a09fc4420546bb478005bb_ebf266926da5edb37b61a9d81d034fb2_Nathan%20M%20SEO.webp"},"datePublished":"2026-03-09T16:56:38.180Z","dateModified":"2026-03-09T16:56:38.180Z","about":{"@type":"Person","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/nathan-mirizzi/#person","name":"Nathan Mirizzi","url":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/nathan-mirizzi"}},{"@type":"Organization","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/#organization","name":"Savvy Wealth","url":"https://www.savvywealth.com/","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6479cdbae84fd9792129c576/647dd6624b8fd164bb0f9637_Savvy%20Logo.svg"},"sameAs":["https://www.linkedin.com/company/savvywealth","https://x.com/SavvyWealthInc"],"contactPoint":[{"@type":"ContactPoint","telephone":"+1-833-745-6789","contactType":"Customer Service","areaServed":"US","availableLanguage":["English"]}]},{"@type":"Person","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/nathan-mirizzi/#person","name":"Nathan Mirizzi","honorificSuffix":"CFP®","jobTitle":"Associate Advisor","image":"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6479cdbae84fd9792129c576/69a09fc4972a96454bb7aa96_Nathan%20M%20Hero%20(1).webp","url":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/nathan-mirizzi","email":"mailto:nathan@bluebarnwealth.com","telephone":"+1-801-797-0497","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Salt Lake City","addressRegion":"UT","addressCountry":"US"},"worksFor":{"@type":"Organization","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/#organization"},"sameAs":["https://www.linkedin.com/in/nathan-mirizzi/"],"knowsAbout":["Financial Planning & Analysis","Tax Optimization","Alternative Investing","Investment Management"],"description":"Nathan Mirizzi is an Associate Advisor at Blue Barn Wealth and a CERTIFIED FINANCIAL PLANNER™ professional. He graduated from California Polytechnic State University, San Luis Obispo, in 2022 with a Bachelor’s Degree in Business Administration, concentrating in Financial Management and Accounting.

Nathan is passionate about personal finance and is dedicated to helping individuals thoughtfully navigate their financial journeys. He approaches both his professional and personal life with enthusiasm and initiative, guided by the motto “Engage in life.”

Outside of work, Nathan enjoys outdoor activities including hiking, camping, skiing, hunting, and fishing, as well as spending quality time with family and friends."},{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://www.savvywealth.com"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Nathan Mirizzi","item":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/nathan-mirizzi"}]},{"@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How did you become a financial advisor?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"I’ve always known I wanted to build a career in personal finance because of the real impact it has on people’s everyday lives. While studying financial management and accounting, that direction became even clearer to me. I realized I didn’t just want to understand the numbers—I wanted to work directly with individuals, helping them feel more confident and in control of their financial decisions."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What types of clients do you work with?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"I work with individuals and families who want to build a strong financial foundation and be intentional about where their wealth can take them. Many clients are navigating increasing complexity—whether that’s investments, career, income, taxes, family planning, or long-term legacy goals—and are looking for clarity, structure, and thoughtful strategy."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What areas of expertise do you have?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"My background includes financial planning fundamentals, investment strategy, and financial analysis. I focus on helping clients understand their options and make disciplined, informed decisions."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What types of strategies do you usually help clients with?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"We offer a comprehensive planning process built around key areas such as financial planning, investment management, tax planning, estate planning, and charitable giving. The goal is to help clients make confident decisions across all parts of their financial life, not just one piece at a time."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is there a unique approach that sets you apart?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"I bring a high level of energy and attention to detail to every client relationship. I believe strong financial planning starts with engagement—understanding each client’s goals and building a strategy that supports them over time."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is your favorite part about working with clients?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Helping clients gain confidence in their financial decisions. When someone feels clear about their plan and empowered to move forward, that’s incredibly rewarding."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Working with Savvy","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Working with Savvy enhances the tools and operational support behind the scenes, allowing our team to deliver a seamless and modern client experience. The platform enables us to focus on thoughtful planning, strong communication, and long-term financial success for the families we serve."}}]}]}

{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"WebSite","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/#website","url":"https://www.savvywealth.com/","name":"Savvy Wealth"},{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/elijah-pell/#webpage","name":"Elijah Pell, AAMS®, CEPA: Wealth Manager in Waterbury, VT | Savvy Wealth","url":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/elijah-pell","description":"Elijah Pell, AAMS®, CEPA is a wealth manager at Savvy Wealth who helps individuals, families, and business owners make confident financial decisions through education-driven, tax-aware planning and long-term partnership.","isPartOf":{"@type":"WebSite","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/#website"},"primaryImageOfPage":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6479cdbae84fd9792129c576/68dbfff07bb1e7b0ee188d92_Elijah%20Pell%20Hero%20(1).webp"},"datePublished":"2025-12-19T02:20:41.111Z","dateModified":"2025-12-19T02:20:41.111Z"},{"@type":"Organization","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/#organization","name":"Savvy Wealth","url":"https://www.savvywealth.com/","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6479cdbae84fd9792129c576/647dd6624b8fd164bb0f9637_Savvy%20Logo.svg"},"sameAs":["https://www.linkedin.com/company/savvywealth","https://x.com/SavvyWealthInc"],"contactPoint":[{"@type":"ContactPoint","telephone":"+1-833-745-6789","contactType":"Customer Service","areaServed":"US","availableLanguage":["English"]}]},{"@type":"Person","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/elijah-pell/#person","name":"Elijah Pell","honorificSuffix":"AAMS®, CEPA","jobTitle":"Wealth Manager","image":"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6479cdbae84fd9792129c576/68dbfff07bb1e7b0ee188d92_Elijah%20Pell%20Hero%20(1).webp","url":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/elijah-pell","email":"mailto:elijah.pell@savvyadvisors.com","telephone":"+1-802-214-1832","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Waterbury","addressRegion":"VT","addressCountry":"US"},"worksFor":{"@type":"Organization","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/#organization"},"sameAs":["https://www.linkedin.com/in/elijahpell/"],"knowsAbout":["Retirement Planning","Tax Optimization","Legacy & Charitable Planning","Financial Planning"],"description":"Elijah brings over eight years of experience in comprehensive financial planning, grounded in a background in accounting, analytics, mutual fund research, and private equity. Early in his career, his work in investment analytics provided deep exposure to markets and portfolio construction—but witnessing the real-world impact of poor financial planning on families shaped his purpose.

Today, Elijah focuses on people over portfolios. His approach emphasizes education, clarity, and trust, helping clients build confidence in their financial decisions. He works closely with retirees and those transitioning into retirement, business owners, and high-income individuals, offering guidance across retirement income planning, tax-aware investing, risk management, business exit strategies, legacy planning, and charitable giving.

Elijah is known for tailoring recommendations to each client’s comfort level, pacing, and decision style—prioritizing understanding and long-term partnership over complexity."},{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://www.savvywealth.com"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Elijah Pell","item":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/elijah-pell"}]},{"@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How did you become a financial advisor?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"After earning a degree in accounting, I began my career in mutual fund analytics and later worked as an analyst in private equity. While the work gave me a strong understanding of markets and investing, witnessing the impact of poor financial planning on families made it clear that I wanted to directly help people. That realization led me into personal financial planning, where I could apply my analytical background to make a meaningful difference in clients’ lives."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What types of clients do you work with?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"I primarily work with retirees and individuals transitioning into retirement who need income distribution planning, Social Security timing guidance, cash flow management, and risk management. I also work with business owners and high-income individuals seeking tax-aware strategies, non-qualified investment management, and coordinated financial planning."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What areas of expertise do you have?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"I specialize in tax-efficient investing for non-qualified brokerage accounts, including asset location strategy, gain and loss harvesting, liquidity planning, and portfolio construction designed to support long-term goals."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What types of strategies do you usually help clients with?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"My primary focus is comprehensive retirement income planning—strategically sequencing withdrawals from taxable, tax-deferred, and Roth accounts, minimizing taxes, and coordinating Required Minimum Distributions (RMDs)."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is there a unique approach that sets you apart?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"I start by deeply understanding each client’s goals, concerns, family dynamics, and decision-making style. I adapt both the pacing and complexity of recommendations to ensure clarity and confidence, building trust through education and thoughtful guidance."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is your favorite part about working with clients?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Building long-term relationships and supporting clients through life’s milestones is what I value most. Seeing plans come together and providing steady guidance through challenges brings real meaning to my work."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Working with Savvy","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Savvy’s collaborative environment and efficient technology reduce administrative friction and allow me to spend more time focused on planning and client relationships, which ultimately leads to better outcomes."}}]}]}

{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"WebSite","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/#website","url":"https://www.savvywealth.com/","name":"Savvy Wealth"},{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/jacob-ray/#webpage","name":"Jacob Ray, AWMA®, AIF®: Wealth Manager in Denver, CO | Savvy Wealth","url":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/jacob-ray","description":"Webpage with info on Jacob Ray, wealth manager at Savvy.","isPartOf":{"@type":"WebSite","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/#website"},"primaryImageOfPage":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6479cdbae84fd9792129c576/696fc09e1be151bd75fbebad_Jacob%20R%20Hero%20(1)-p-500.webp"},"datePublished":"2026-01-29T16:04:21.363Z","dateModified":"2026-01-29T16:04:21.363Z"},{"@type":"Organization","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/#organization","name":"Savvy Wealth","url":"https://www.savvywealth.com/","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6479cdbae84fd9792129c576/647dd6624b8fd164bb0f9637_Savvy%20Logo.svg"},"sameAs":["https://www.linkedin.com/company/savvywealth","https://x.com/SavvyWealthInc"],"contactPoint":[{"@type":"ContactPoint","telephone":"+1-833-745-6789","contactType":"Customer Service","areaServed":"US","availableLanguage":["English"]}]},{"@type":"Person","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/jacob-ray/#person","name":"Jacob Ray","honorificSuffix":"AWMA®, AIF®","jobTitle":"Wealth Manager","image":"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6479cdbae84fd9792129c576/696fc09e1be151bd75fbebad_Jacob%20R%20Hero%20(1)-p-500.webp","url":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/jacob-ray","email":"mailto:jray@coloradowealthgroup.com","telephone":"+1-720-729-2504","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Denver","addressRegion":"CO","addressCountry":"US"},"worksFor":{"@type":"Organization","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/#organization"},"sameAs":["https://www.linkedin.com/in/jacobray7/"],"knowsAbout":["Retirement Planning","Financial Planning & Analysis","Income Planning"],"description":"Jacob brings over a decade of experience in the financial services industry to his role at Colorado Wealth Group. He holds a Bachelor’s degree in Business Administration from the University of Northern Colorado and an MBA from Western Kentucky University.

Jacob’s professional designations include Accredited Wealth Management Advisor (AWMA®) and Accredited Investment Fiduciary (AIF®). These credentials, combined with his experience, support comprehensive, tailored financial planning and investment guidance for each client’s unique situation.

Outside of work, Jacob enjoys spending time with his wife, Leanne, and their children. They love exploring Colorado’s outdoors, trying new restaurants and breweries, and spending time with family and friends."},{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://www.savvywealth.com"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Jacob Ray","item":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/jacob-ray"}]},{"@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How did you become a financial advisor?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"I’ve always been drawn to helping people make informed, confident financial decisions. Over the past decade in financial services, I’ve focused on building the skills and experience necessary to guide clients through complex financial landscapes and help them achieve their goals."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What types of clients do you work with?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"I work with individuals, families, and business owners who want comprehensive, strategic planning that accounts for their unique financial circumstances, including retirement, stock option divestitures, and education planning."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What areas of expertise do you have?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"My expertise lies in financial planning and investment management, with an emphasis on retirement planning, cash flow analysis, risk management, and company stock/divestiture strategies. I focus on helping clients integrate all aspects of their financial lives into one cohesive plan."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What types of strategies do you usually help clients with?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"I help clients develop strategies for retirement planning, cash flow management, company stock option divestitures, tax-efficient wealth management, and education planning. Each plan is tailored to the client’s goals and circumstances."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is there a unique approach that sets you apart?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"I bring a combination of attention to detail, critical insight, and practical guidance to every client relationship. My approach is collaborative and transparent, helping clients understand their options, feel confident in their decisions, and stay on track toward their goals."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is your favorite part about working with clients?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"I enjoy helping clients see the big picture come together. Watching a plan take shape and knowing it provides clarity and peace of mind is the most rewarding part of my work. I value building long-term relationships and being a trusted partner through all of life’s financial milestones."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Working with Savvy","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Savvy’s platform enables our team at Colorado Wealth Group to provide high-touch, fiduciary-focused service with the support of modern, integrated technology. The collaborative tools and real-time dashboards allow us to focus on strategy, insight, and personalized guidance—so clients can see and understand their full financial picture in one place."}}]}]}

{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"name":"Savvy Wealth","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/#website","@type":"WebSite","url":"https://www.savvywealth.com"},{"datePublished":"2026-04-29T16:29:31.859Z","primaryImageOfPage":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6479cdbae84fd9792129c576/69ea60407beb2be3aa112812_Lindsey%20L%20SEO.webp"},"@type":"WebPage","about":{"name":"Lindsey Lewis, MBA, ChFC®, CFP®","@type":"Person","url":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/lindsey-lewis"},"name":"Lindsey Lewis, MBA, ChFC®, CFP®: Financial Advisor in Park City and Salt Lake City, UT | Savvy Wealth","description":"Financial advisor Lindsey Lewis of Blue Barn Wealth helps high-net-worth individuals, entrepreneurs, and athletes simplify complex finances with personalized planning, tax strategies, and investment management.","dateModified":"2026-04-29T16:29:31.859Z","isPartOf":{"@type":"WebSite","url":"https://www.savvywealth.com"},"url":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/lindsey-lewis"},{"contactPoint":[{"contactType":"Customer Service","telephone":"+1-833-745-6789","areaServed":"US","@type":"ContactPoint","availableLanguage":["English"]}],"@type":"Organization","name":"Savvy Wealth","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6479cdbae84fd9792129c576/647dd6624b8fd164bb0f9637_Savvy%20Logo.svg"},"@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/#organization","url":"https://www.savvywealth.com","sameAs":["https://www.linkedin.com/company/savvywealth","https://x.com/SavvyWealthInc"]},{"image":"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6479cdbae84fd9792129c576/69ea603f3480eb13a570971b_Lindsey%20L%20Hero%20(1).webp","address":{"addressCountry":"US","addressLocality":"Park City and Salt Lake City","addressRegion":"UT","@type":"PostalAddress"},"knowsAbout":["Financial Planning & Analysis","Tax Optimization","Alternative Investing","​​Investment Management"],"worksFor":{"name":"Savvy Wealth","@type":"Organization","url":"https://www.savvywealth.com"},"@type":"Person","jobTitle":"Financial Advisor","description":"Lindsey Lewis, MBA, ChFC®, CFP®, is a Park City-based financial advisor with Blue Barn Wealth, known for helping clients simplify complex financial lives and make confident decisions through moments that matter most. She works with high-net-worth individuals and families, entrepreneurs, and professional athletes, guiding them through growth, success, and transition with clarity, structure, and intention.

In addition to her advisory work, Lindsey serves as Managing Director at The American College of Financial Services, where she is focused on shaping the future of financial advice and developing the next generation of professionals. She also contributes to Advisor Launch Lab, supporting the development of advisors as they build and grow their practices. Her work has earned national recognition, including InvestmentNews Hot List in 2025 and 2023, as well as the InvestmentNews Trailblazer Award and other industry honors recognizing her impact on the profession.

Outside of her professional work, Lindsey brings the same level of energy and intention to her personal life. She is a mom of two, a yoga teacher, and someone who prioritizes strength, movement, and balance, values that carry through to how she approaches both life and wealth.","telephone":"(801) 871-8710","url":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/lindsey-lewis","honorificSuffix":"MBA, ChFC®, CFP®","name":"Lindsey Lewis","email":"mailto:lindsey@bluebarnwealth.com","sameAs":["https://www.linkedin.com/in/lindseycarolyn/"]},{"itemListElement":[{"name":"Home","item":"https://www.savvywealth.com","position":1,"@type":"ListItem"},{"name":"Lindsey Lewis","item":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/lindsey-lewis","position":2,"@type":"ListItem"}],"@type":"BreadcrumbList"},{"mainEntity":[{"name":"How did you become a financial advisor?","@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"I started my career at the intersection of women and money, after seeing how transformative financial confidence can be. That work gave me a deep understanding of how people think, feel, and make decisions about money. Over time, that foundation expanded into a broader advisory practice where I now work with individuals and families navigating complexity, growth, and transition. The common thread has always been helping clients make informed decisions, simplify complexity, and move forward with confidence."}},{"name":"What types of clients do you work with?","@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"I work with high-net-worth individuals and families, entrepreneurs, and professional athletes who are navigating growth, success, or meaningful life transitions. Many of my clients are balancing multiple priorities and looking for a trusted partner to help them simplify decisions and think strategically about their financial lives. While my career began with a focus on women, that perspective continues to inform how I approach advice today, bringing a more thoughtful, relationship-driven experience to a broader range of clients."}},{"name":"Is there a unique approach that sets you apart?","@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"I take an integrated, experience-driven approach to financial planning. That means going beyond transactions and helping clients think through how their financial decisions connect to their life, priorities, and long-term vision. My background at the intersection of women and money shaped how I communicate and guide decisions, and today that perspective allows me to simplify complex situations and help clients move forward with clarity and confidence."}},{"name":"Working with Savvy","@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Working with Savvy allows me to combine personalized advice with modern technology and infrastructure. It creates a more seamless and efficient client experience while keeping the focus where it belongs on thoughtful planning, strong relationships, and long-term outcomes."}},{"name":"What areas of expertise do you have?","@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"My work centers on comprehensive financial planning, investment strategy, and helping clients navigate complex financial decisions with clarity. I focus on connecting all aspects of a client’s financial life so each decision supports a cohesive, long-term strategy. In addition to my client work, I bring industry leadership experience focused on advisor development, evolving client needs, and the future of financial advice."}},{"name":"What types of strategies do you usually help clients with?","@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"I help clients with a wide range of planning needs, including investment strategy, retirement planning, and structuring their financial lives in a more intentional and organized way. Many of the conversations I guide are tied to pivotal moments such as business growth, liquidity events, or life transitions like divorce. My role is to simplify those decisions, bring structure to the process, and ensure each step aligns with a broader long-term plan."}},{"name":"What is your favorite part about working with clients?","@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"My favorite part is seeing the shift that happens when clarity replaces uncertainty. When clients understand their options and begin making decisions with confidence and intention, it changes not just their financial lives, but how they show up in other areas as well. Being part of that process is incredibly meaningful."}}],"@type":"FAQPage"}]}

{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"WebSite","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/#website","url":"https://www.savvywealth.com","name":"Savvy Wealth"},{"@type":"WebPage","name":"Allen Buckley, CFP®: Wealth Manager in Franklin, TN | Savvy Wealth","url":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/allen-buckley","about":{"@type":"Person","name":"Allen Buckley, CFP®","url":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/allen-buckley"},"isPartOf":{"@type":"WebSite","url":"https://www.savvywealth.com"},"primaryImageOfPage":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6479cdbae84fd9792129c576/69f1e5e061b5ed79c60439f3_Allen%20B%20Hero%20(1).webp"},"datePublished":"2026-06-24T14:12:54.529Z","dateModified":"2026-06-24T14:12:54.529Z","description":"CFP® with over two decades of experience serving high-net-worth families, Allen Buckley delivers deeply personalized wealth management tailored to each client's goals and circumstances."},{"@type":"Organization","@id":"https://www.savvywealth.com/#organization","name":"Savvy Wealth","url":"https://www.savvywealth.com","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6479cdbae84fd9792129c576/647dd6624b8fd164bb0f9637_Savvy%20Logo.svg"},"sameAs":["https://www.linkedin.com/company/savvywealth","https://x.com/SavvyWealthInc"],"contactPoint":[{"@type":"ContactPoint","telephone":"+1-833-745-6789","contactType":"Customer Service","areaServed":"US","availableLanguage":["English"]}]},{"@type":"Person","name":"Allen Buckley","honorificSuffix":"CFP®","jobTitle":"Wealth Manager","image":"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6479cdbae84fd9792129c576/69f1e5e061b5ed79c60439f3_Allen%20B%20Hero%20(1).webp","url":"https://www.savvywealth.com/advisor-directory/allen-buckley","email":"mailto:allen.buckley@savvyadvisors.com","telephone":"(516) 323-1048","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Franklin","addressRegion":"TN","addressCountry":"US"},"description":"Allen Buckley has over two decades of experience in finance serving the unique needs of high net-worth and ultra high net-worth families. As a Certified Financial Planner™, he specializes in helping clients achieve their financial goals, tailored to their individual circumstances and aspirations.

As a former Vice President in personal financial management at one of the world’s leading investment banks, Allen gained invaluable insights into managing wealth for discerning clients. During his tenure at Goldman Sachs, Allen worked with individual clients and families, helped them navigate complex financial landscapes and tailored financial solutions to their specific needs.

